RF.put("questb:b48",{"8848":{"id":8848,"t":"Fifteen Signets for War Supplies","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"15 Alliance Commendation Signet","rew":"You will receive:\nAhn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.5,"y":34.7,"n":"Field Marshal Snowfall","s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8528":{"id":8528,"t":"The Alliance Needs Spotted Yellowtail!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 42.","obj":"Bring 20 Spotted Yellowtail to Huntress Swiftriver at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n20 Spotted Yellowtail Raene Wolfrunner 0.7 % , Volcor 0.7 % , Terenthis 0.7 % , Sentinel Selarin 0.7 % and 4 more","desc":"It may not seem heroic to gather up cooked fish, but do not underestimate the value of preparation, young ‹class›. Soldiers need to eat like anyone else, and we're here to do our part to make sure they have what they need once the war in Ahn'Qiraj commences.\nAccordingly, I am stockpiling spotted yellowtail, a versatile source of sustenance that stores well and can be used in many different dishes. It also doesn't have the odor of some other saltwater fish. Are you willing to aid me in this endeavor?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"I am confident that you are returning so soon with the spotted yellowtail we discussed.","done":"Thank you for this gift, ‹class›, and in such a timely manner as well. Our soldiers will surely not lack for something to eat. Just let me get these fish stored away properly and then you and I can discuss a second haul if you're willing.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.6,"y":32.2,"n":"Huntress Swiftriver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8608":{"id":8608,"t":"The Horde Needs More Mageweave Bandages!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Mageweave Bandages to Lady Callow at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Mageweave Bandage","desc":"You returned? Interesting. As you can see I am still collecting for the Ahn'Qiraj 'war effort'. Which means that I need you to once again go out and collect a stack of mageweave bandages for me. I look forward to your return, ‹class›.","rew":"You will receive:\n7 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","done":"Astounding, ‹class›, you actually did it again! Well, they do say that I have good taste in those that I choose to place in my service. Very well, your contribution is noted and you will receive the social benefits that your efforts have afforded. I suggest though that you go back out and gather yet another bundle of mageweave bandages if you truly wish to prove your worth.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.2,"y":75.1,"n":"Lady Callow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"6848":{"id":6848,"t":"Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 50 instead of 51.","obj":"Recover Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye from the Winterax caves and return it to Master Ryson.\nBe warned, it is said that Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye carries with it a terrible curse!","desc":"Your war in the heart of Alterac means nothing to the Syndicate, ‹class›. We will do as we have always done: Wait until a clear victor rises from the ashes and rubble of this madness and then strike.\nThat, however, is not why we are here now. The All Seeing Eye has been lost - taken by the Winterax trolls of the region.\nRecover the Eye and our services shall be yours - for whatever time remains for your side.\nReturn to me once you acquire the eye so that I may examine you.\n<Master Ryson grins.>\nStart Syndicate Master Ryson Alterac Valley End Syndicate Master Ryson Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 56 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6848","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7168":{"id":7168,"t":"Rise and Be Recognized","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Stormpike Insignia Rank 1","desc":"Most do not live long enough to rise above their own mediocrity. You have proven yourself to be an exemplary soldier, ‹class›. The time has come.\nPresent your insignia.","rew":"You will receive:\nStormpike Insignia Rank 2\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Most do not live long enough to rise above their own mediocrity. You have proven yourself to be an exemplary soldier, ‹class›. The time has come.\nPresent your insignia.","done":"Let our enemies see that a soldier of rank has struck them down! Fight for the glory of Stormpike!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Lieutenant Haggerdin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"688":{"id":688,"t":"Myzrael's Allies","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Zaruk in Hammerfall.","desc":"<Myzrael speaks.>\nFree! I AM FREE! I am free to gather strength, hidden from my captors. For if they faced me now they would surely overpower and again imprison me.\nBut in time I will confront the giants, and they will regret their wardship of me!\nYou are a noble ally, ‹name›. I will need your help again in time. When I am ready, I will need you to summon me to the surface\nSpeak with Zaruk in Hammerfall. He knows how I can be summoned.","rew":"Experience: 2,350","done":"Welcome, ‹class›. The Lady has informed me of your coming, and if we are to bring her back to the surface then we have much to discuss...","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":36.1,"y":58.1,"n":"Keystone","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.5,"y":35.6,"n":"Zaruk","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1008":{"id":1008,"t":"The Zoram Strand","lv":19,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Wrathtail Heads to Shindrell Swiftfire in Astranaar.\n20 Wrathtail Head Wrathtail Priestess , Wrathtail Sorceress , Wrathtail Sea Witch , Wrathtail Wave Rider and 2 more","desc":"There is evil lurking on our northwestern coast, known as the Zoram Strand.\nIt is the resting place of the doomed city of Zoram, destroyed during the Sundering and submerged beneath the seas. It has been lost to the night elves for ages. Lost, and nearly forgotten.\nNow, the naga have returned, and for what reason we do not know. But reason matters little; we must slay these fiends and throw them back to the depths!\nReturn to me when your mission is complete.","rew":"Money: 11 0 gold, 11 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,450\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"We cannot allow the naga to invade our coasts, ‹name›. It is vital that you go to the Zoram Strand and complete your mission.","done":"Very well done, ‹name›. Your actions in the Zoram Strand against the naga are commendable.\nI know your feat was not easily accomplished, for the strength and guile of the naga is well known to the night elves. We know this, for we share a history with them.\nIt is a history I care not to repeat.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":34.7,"y":48.8,"n":"Shindrell Swiftfire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"4128":{"id":4128,"t":"Ragnar Thunderbrew","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Ragnar Thunderbrew.","desc":"Ho, ‹name›. I heard that Ragnar Thunderbrew is steaming mad about someone stealing his ale. He's looking for stalwart adventurers, and willing to pay plenty.\nTalk to Ragnar if you're interested. He's at the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos, in Dun Morogh.","rew":"Experience: 550","done":"You're right I'm mad! I've been robbed! Robbed of one of our family recipes! How dare they! As if I didn't have enough cause to hate the Dark Iron dwarves! Now, oh... now they're in for it!\nBlasted Lands Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":63.6,"y":20.6,"n":"Enohar Thunderbrew","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.8,"y":52.4,"n":"Ragnar Thunderbrew","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4768":{"id":4768,"t":"The Darkstone Tablet","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Darkstone Tablet to Shadow Mage Vivian Lagrave in Kargath.\nDarkstone Tablet Darkstone Tablet","desc":"The Darkstone Tablet holds the writings of the long-dead dwarf Urheld Darkstone. An alchemist of great skill, he was thought insane by his contemporaries and, hence, did not share his research.\nBut he did etch it onto tablets, and I believe one such tablet lies in Blackrock Spire, in a chamber once named the Hall of Fortune. I know not what it is now called, for few enter Blackrock and return.\nBut if you are willing to brave its dangers and return to me with the tablet, your reward will be great.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSwiftfoot Treads Blinkstrike Armguards\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you found the Tablet, ‹name›? I yearn to delve into its secrets.","done":"Excellent. The formulae etched into this tablet will consume days of research, but I am confident such research will bear sweet fruit.\nThank you, ‹name›. You have been invaluable to us.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":2.9,"y":47.8,"n":"Shadowmage Vivian Lagrave","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"8288":{"id":8288,"t":"Only One May Rise","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Head of the Broodlord Lashlayer to Baristolth of the Shifting Sands at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.\nHead of the Broodlord Lashlayer Broodlord Lashlayer in Blackwing Lair","desc":"There is no time to waste! A hero must be found! The task I give will require an army to complete but only one may rise from the throng of would be champions to take on the burden and responsibility of an ally of the Brood.\nWithin the lair of the Lord of Blackrock is a most cruel beast. The Broodlord Lashlayer guards the Halls of Strife, blocking the way into Nefarian's inner sanctum. Slay the foul aberration and return his head to me. Do this and you may begin the next step of your journey.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"It is the favor of the Brood of Nozdormu that you must earn.","done":"Could you be the first to earn favor among the Bronze Flight in a thousand years?","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.5,"y":36.4,"n":"Baristolth of the Shifting Sands","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackwing-lair"]},"97968":{"id":97968,"t":"Camping 101 herbalism","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Syriel Nightrain in Valanaar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your herbalism skill to 20","desc":"Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Incense Candle. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":57.8,"y":75.4,"n":"Syriel Nightrain","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96608":{"id":96608,"t":"The great outdoors","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Sit near Eric's Basic Campfire by typing /sit in the chat window and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.\nUse the /sit emote near the campfire\nGain the Boosted Rest buff","desc":"Greetings, ‹class›. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.","back":"Having the skills needed to survive the outdoors are critical. A well-rested and well-prepared adventurer has a much higher chance of surviving this lifestyle.","done":"So now that we've learned the basics, why don't you go and learn a tradeskill from the trainers in the village nearby. They will also teach you how to create a camp fixture suitable to your new profession.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.6,"y":53.8,"n":"Eric Brighthammer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94288":{"id":94288,"t":"Craftsmans writ mithril frag bomb","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Mithril Frag Bomb\nMithril Frag Bomb","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Mithril Frag Bomb, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Mithril Frag Bomb Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94288","cats":["crafting"]},"1488":{"id":1488,"t":"The Corrupter","lv":40,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Lord Azrethoc and Jugkar Grim'rod and return to Takata Steelblade in Desolace.\nLord Azrethoc slain\nJugkar Grim'rod slain","desc":"Although I have no knowledge of this Lord Azrethoc, I agree with Maurin, he must be stopped; especially if he is attempting to gain influence over the Burning Blade to further his goals.\nYou have already shown you wish to aid the Warchief, and I would trust you to gather a party to slay the demon lord and his warlock servant.\nWhen you are ready, head directly south, and return to me when the threat has been ended.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBasalt Buckler Enforcer Pauldrons\nExperience: 3,900\n+150 reputation with Horde","back":"Glory to the Horde, and death to our enemies, ‹name›!\nThe demons in Desolace pose a greater threat than ever before. My hope of returning to the Warchief dwindles as more and more of the foul creatures seem to appear.\nI sometimes wish it was only the centaur we had to deal with.","done":"A mighty victory for us all, ‹name›. Let us rejoice in your success. I trust now that our future here is not as bleak as I once thought.\nThe demons will be slain, the Burning Blade will fail in their efforts, and we may one day have a place we can safely call home again.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":52.6,"y":54.4,"n":"Takata Steelblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"7488":{"id":7488,"t":"Lethtendris's Web","lv":57,"min":54,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Lethtendris' Web to Latronicus Moonspear at the Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas.\nLethtendris's Web Lethtendris","desc":"The mage Lethtendris, a vicious blood elf whose brutality is matched only by her twisted addiction to magic, has fled into Dire Maul. She has created a device, a web to ensnare the magical energies of that place and we fear that, if left unchecked, she will cause irreparable damage to our world!\nStop her, ‹name›. Find her and retrieve her web. She is likely near the satyrs in Warpwood Quarter of Dire Maul. Bring the web to me so that its power may be released safely back into the wilds...","rew":"You will receive:\nLorespinner\nMoney: 1 70 1 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,550\n+150 reputation with Alliance","back":"Do you have the web, ‹name›? Its concentrated magical energy must be dissipated!","done":"You retrieved the web! Well done, ‹name›! Lethtendris, like many elves of her ilk, are blind to the dangers the abuse of magic can cause to our world. They believe they are masters of magic; they do not realize that they are slaves to their own addiction. Her death saddens me, but it was necessary.\nThank you, ‹name›. I will have the energies within the web released safely over a wide area, and then I'll destroy it to prevent future magical exploits.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.4,"y":46.2,"n":"Latronicus Moonspear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dire-maul"]},"6128":{"id":6128,"t":"Gathering the Cure","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Earthroot and 5 Kodo Horns to Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads so he may make a curative salve.\n5 Earthroot Earthroot , Earthroot , Tattered Chest 6 % , Battered Chest 6 % and 4 more\n5 Kodo Horn Lost Barrens Kodo 80 % , Barrens Kodo 80 %","desc":"The water will serve as the base of the curative salve I shall make for the gazelles. For curative properties, I need some earthroot. Herbalists know how to find it, so if you are not familiar with this skill you'll need to find one to help us out.\nFinally for potency, I need kodo horns - mere chips and fragments will not suffice. Kodos you can handle wander the northern part of the Barrens; bring some down for the greater good of the balance ‹name›, and fetch the horns for me.","rew":"Experience: 750\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Have you got the reagents I need to make the salve? The gazelle aren't getting any better on their own, so we better not tarry in our effort to save them!","done":"This is good, ‹name›, so much so that it should be enough to make some ample doses of the salve - at least enough to start to make a difference.\nMaking a cure for poisons can be quite difficult at times because each one often requires a very specific antidote to counteract it. Imagine being able to cure a poison at will without having to worry about the exact ingredients of what the antidote must be!\nNow, let me get to work on this!","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.3,"y":31.9,"n":"Tonga Runetotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"1168":{"id":1168,"t":"Army of the Black Dragon","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,600 experience instead of 4,450, 0.81 times as much.","obj":"Tharg in Brackenwall Village wants you to kill 10 Firemane Scouts, 10 Firemane Ash Tails, and 5 Firemane Scalebanes.\nFiremane Scout slain : 0/ 10\nFiremane Ash Tail slain : 0/ 10\nFiremane Scalebane slain : 0/ 5","desc":"Mok'Morokk was made Overlord by Rexxar. He care more for power than he care for ogres.\nBlack dragons kill many ogre. Kill Tharg's wife. Mok'Morokk tell us to run. Make us come here.\nOgre should fight. Ogres not good at running. Mok'Morokk care only about Mok'Morokk.\nMe call Stonemaul Ruins home. Me like it in the south. This place not home.\nHelp ogres fight army of the black dragon. Me want revenge. Me want to go home.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTharg's Shoelace Tharg's Disk\nExperience: 3,600","back":"Mok'Morokk tell all ogres to stay and keep this place safe. Me think ogres need to kill black dragon army and get old home back.\nYou help ogres get home back. Help ogres get revenge.","done":"You kill many of the black dragon army. You brave ‹race›.\nMake Tharg happy.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":37.4,"y":31.4,"n":"Tharg","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5168":{"id":5168,"t":"Heroes of Darrowshire","lv":56,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Davil's Libram and Redpath's Shield to Carlin Redpath.\nDavil's Libram Davil's Libram\nRedpath's Shield Redpath's Shield","desc":"The heroes of Darrowshire hold a place in my heart, and the book you brought me, the Annals of Darrowshire, tells their tales.\nIt tells of the paladin Davil Lightfire and how the Crusade took his libram to the town hall of Hearthglen.\nIts passages also speak of my brother, Captain Redpath. After his betrayal, his shield was cracked and discarded and now lies in the most unlikely of places -- near the barn of Gahrron's Withering.\nGather these relics, ‹name›. For fate and tragedy surrounds them.","rew":"Experience: 5,800","back":"Do you have the relics, ‹name›?","done":"You have the libram and the shield!\nTheir history is entwined with the history of Darrowshire, and somehow, I know that fate will bring them together again.\nEastern Plaguelands Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":50,"n":"Carlin Redpath","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"5248":{"id":5248,"t":"Tormented By the Past","lv":58,"min":53,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Crystal of Zin-Malor to Lake Kel'Theril in Winterspring and find a highborne spirit that will speak to you.\nCrystal of Zin-Malor\nProvided: Crystal of Zin-Malor","desc":"‹name›, I weep for what has happened in the past. Like this crystal, the elves, as a race, have been shattered. I do not know if the pieces will ever again be reunited into one, but my sorrow has been eased by being able to help you with this one small task.\nWe must not forget the past, ‹name›...\nPlease take the Crystal of Zin-Malor back to Lake Kel'Theril. You must find a highborne spirit that realizes the error of what was done so long ago. Show the spirit that we have made things right again.","rew":"Experience: 4,650\n+25 reputation with Alliance","back":"Currrrrsed... Forevvvverrrr...","done":"Pleeease, leeeave meeeeee...\nEastern Plaguelands Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":46.5,"y":16,"n":"Aurora Skycaller","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":56.1,"y":44.4,"n":"Remorseful Highborne","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"4448":{"id":4448,"t":"Corrupted Night Dragon","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a Night Dragon plant. The fruits that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply 4 Cenarion Plant Salves to the Night Dragon. It immediately begins to shed it's corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":42.5,"y":13.9,"n":"Corrupted Night Dragon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"5888":{"id":5888,"t":"Salve via Mining","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Tainted Vitriol Gold Vein 50 % , Ooze Covered Gold Vein 50 % , Gold Vein 50 % , Mithril Deposit 50 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"If you possess a Cenarion beacon while mining in Felwood, you will be able to see tainted vitriol that corrupts a vein of raw metal. I know how to purify that vitriol and turn it into a reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. You will then use that salve on plants you find in the wild that need saving.\nIf you have collected any tainted vitriol, I'll give you some Cenarion plant salve I have already prepared.","done":"Very well then, here's some Cenarion plant salve. If you find more vitriol when you mine in Felwood, remember to hold on to it for me! The more of it you find, the more salve I will be able to make.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":46.7,"y":83.1,"n":"Maybess Riverbreeze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"6608":{"id":6608,"t":"You Too Good.","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"You think Lumak is trying to tell you that he can no longer help you improve your fishing skill. You may want to try to find his friend, Nat Pagle, a human fishing off one of the islands south of Theramore (at least that's what you think Lumak said).","desc":"Lumak no can teach ‹name› no more. You too good! Find Lumak friend, Nat Pagle. Is human but no eat! Is Lumak friend! Nat teach you fish gooder.\nYou find Nat in Dustwallow Marsh, south of Humie town, Thermorosomethinglikedat. Nat probably fishing. Go now!","rew":"Experience: 975","done":"'Course, you must be a friend of Lumak's.\nFishin'? I can tell you all 'bout fishin'.\nOrgrimmar Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":69.8,"y":29.2,"n":"Lumak","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":58.6,"y":60.1,"n":"Nat Pagle","e":1}],"cats":["fishing"]},"2928":{"id":2928,"t":"Gyrodrillmatic Excavationators","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 4,400 experience instead of 2,450, 1.8 times as much. New rewards: Operator's Gloves. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a no","obj":"Bring twenty-four Robo-mechanical Guts to Shoni in Stormwind.\n24 Robo-mechanical Guts Techbot , Leprous Assistant 80 % , Irradiated Pillager 80 % , Mechanized Guardian 80 % and 4 more","desc":"It's terrible, ‹name›. We are not going to have enough parts to get our fleet of gyrodrillmatic excavationators to Dun Morogh.\nWhat we need are spare parts, ‹name›. What better place to get the spare parts for our vehicles than Gnomeregan? I hear that bots and mechs roam around that place like cattle on an open range.\nWhat I need you to do is go to Gnomeregan and tear apart those robots. Bring me back their robot guts. Two dozen should be sufficient.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nShoni's Disarming Tool Shilly Mitts Operator's Gloves\nNew in Forever: Operator's Gloves.\nExperience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Stormwind\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"If this were a race, you would have lost by now.","done":"This will do nicely, ‹name›. One gyrodrillmatic excavationator fixed; 398 left to go.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.6,"y":34.1,"n":"Shoni the Shilent","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"528":{"id":528,"t":"Battle of Hillsbrad","lv":25,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 15 Hillsbrad Peasants and report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill.\nHillsbrad Peasant slain : 0/ 15","desc":"Word of the attack on the northern farms has the townsfolk panicked. Most excellent.\nOur Deathstalkers report peasants fleeing to the fields in southern Hillsbrad. The fools think they can hide in the orchards and escape their doom.\nProve them wrong, ‹name›. Return to Hillsbrad Fields and seek out the cowering peasants. Lay waste to them in the name of our Dark Lady.\nDismissed!","rew":"Money: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,000\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"You have your orders, ‹class›. Quit dawdling here in Tarren Mill when there is work to be done elsewhere.","done":"The grip of death is tightening around the town of Hillsbrad. The battle goes well.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.3,"y":20.5,"n":"High Executor Darthalia","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"7808":{"id":7808,"t":"A Donation of Silk","lv":60,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Silk Cloth Protector Weaver , Mountaineer Langarr 85.7 % , Watcher Wollpert 85.7 % , Mountaineer Zwarn 78.3 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+150 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"As with most other fabrics, our stocks of silk are at an all-time low. Our stores are such that we'd only need sixty pieces of silk from you total; we should be able to reach our goal with the support of others.\nA benevolent gift such as silk, might I add, would certainly increase your local standing in the community! If you have the sixty pieces of silk cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63,"y":28.8,"n":"Bubulo Acerbus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"2848":{"id":2848,"t":"Wild Leather Shoulders","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Thick Armor Kits and a Wildvine to Pratt McGrubben in Feathermoon Stronghold.\n6 Thick Armor Kit Olaf 0 %\nWildvine Retherokk the Berserker 80.6 % , Zul'arek Hatefowler 65.1 % , Purple Lotus 10 % , Vilebranch Aman'zasi Guard 9.5 % and 4 more","desc":"Wild Leather shoulders support the wearer's frame extremely well, offering top notch protection of the upper arms and the shoulders themselves. As with all Wild Leather armor, a potent but random benefit is applied to the item as the wildvine is stitched in.\nFor this pattern, I will require six thick armor kits and a wildvine. That shouldn't be too tall of an order for you to fill.","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Wild Leather Shoulders\nExperience: 2,900","back":"Do you have the six thick armor kits and the wildvine I require?\nDon't think of making armor kits as monotonous work; the steady fashioning method you develop as you ply your trade on these kits helps develop your skills for the intricate work needed to make Wild Leather armor.\nSee - there's a real reason behind what you're making for me...","done":"These armor kits are of solid quality, ‹name›. If there is one thing I demand in not only my work, but the work of those in my employ, it is quality.\nYou've done well to earn this pattern; I hope it brings you the rewards it has brought me.\nGains","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.6,"y":42.7,"n":"Pratt McGrubben","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"8688":{"id":8688,"t":"Windrun the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":34.1,"y":64.1,"n":"Elder Windrun","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9088":{"id":9088,"t":"Dreamwalker Headpiece","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rayne at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Dreamwalker Headpiece if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Headpiece, 15 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 6 Cured Rugged Hides and 2 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Headpiece\n15 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n6 Cured Rugged Hide\n2 Nexus Crystal","desc":"Many heroes fell in the last war and many continue to perish at the hands of the Scourge to this day. From the corpses of the fallen, the armor is stripped and taken back to Naxxramas to be used for unknown purposes.\nRecover the desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps and supply to me the other material components I require and I will craft Dreamwalker armor.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreamwalker Headpiece\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"The material cost is high, but soon forgotten.","done":"Your Dreamwalker Headpiece is ready, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Rayne","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9008":{"id":9008,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Mokvar your Beaststalker's Cap and Beaststalker's Tunic.\nBeaststalker's Cap Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nBeaststalker's Tunic General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"A truly amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved, I can assure you. Through your efforts we are delivered from the mistakes of our past.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you have definitely earned and will truly enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nBeastmaster's Cap Beastmaster's Tunic\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Beaststalker pieces in exchange for your new Beastmaster's Cap and Tunic?","done":"I will truly miss you, ‹name›. There is a debt that I owe you, which I may never be able to repay.\nEnjoy your new head and chest armor. May it protect you for a long time to come, and help you to achieve even greater honor!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1648":{"id":1648,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":13,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Linen Cloth to John Turner in Ironforge.\n10 Linen Cloth Kogan Forgestone , Lisan Pierce , Adam Lind 66.7 % , Hidden Strongbox 58.6 % and 4 more","desc":"My wife and I run an orphanage in Stormwind, mostly for children who have lost parents due to the attacks by the Scourge in the last decade. I come to Ironforge every month or so to see about collecting more supplies from the citizens here, and talk to the various groups to see if they can do anything to help.\nThis trip's been agonizingly slow, and not very productive.\nIf I could just get some more linen for my wife to make some clothes, I could finally send a shipment home.","rew":"Experience: 900","back":"What with the influx of tradesmen here and throughout Azeroth, there's a smaller supply of items we use to make clothes for the children of our orphanage. Helping me collect linen so my wife can make new clothes for them is very noble of you, ‹name›. Thank you.\nHopefully, I'll be able to return home to my wife soon.","done":"This is so wonderful of you, ‹name›. Thank you again.\nYou're a noble man for doing this for me. It's no wonder you've chosen to follow the Light. I wish there was some way I could repay you for all you've done... what's that? It's the least you could do? See? That's what I'm talking about, ‹name›, noble to the end.\nBe safe, and may the Light protect you in your travels.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54.8,"y":31,"n":"John Turner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"7648":{"id":7648,"t":"Grimand's Finest Work","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Arcanite Barding to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind's Cathedral District for his inspection.\nArcanite Barding\nProvided: Arcanite Barding","desc":"<Grimand wipes sweat from his brow, beaming with a sense of pride.>\nThere you are, my friend. This is some of my finest work - as good as the barding I personally made for Lord Shadowbreaker when he went for his own charger. I thank you for your trust in me to provide for you the best.\nNo doubt Grayson will want to see the work for himself as well. Take your barding to him, and give him my thanks for his honorable business.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You're progressing along nicely, ‹name›. Once you have made your barding, you'll be well on your way to the next task.","done":"This is most impressive work. It seems that as Grimand gets older, his craftsmanship continues to improve. That's quite the feat when his work was already some of the finest you'd find anywhere when he made my barding back in the day.\nWhile this barding would be a fine addition to any normal steed, we are not dealing with such a mundane beast. You'll need this barding blessed by an appropriate source for it to be worthy of resting on a ‹class›'s charger. I'll hold onto it for you until then.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":59.7,"y":33.8,"n":"Grimand Elmore","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.4,"y":50.2,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5648":{"id":5648,"t":"Garments of Spirituality","lv":4,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Grunt Kor'ja and heal her wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant her Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Tai'jin at Razor Hill.\nHeal and fortify Grunt Kor'ja","desc":"You be ready for your first test, ‹name›. South of Razor Hill, just outta town, one of our grunts be hurt fightin' off some o' Proudmoore's old troops. She not doin' too well, an' she benefit much if one of our kind could help her. Find her--her name be Kor'ja--heal her wounds, an' give her the blessin' of our ancestors.\nYou do this, an' me thinks that be sufficient proof that you ready to move on in our ways.","rew":"You will receive:\nJuju Hex Robes\nExperience: 270","back":"Most think it logical that healin' magics be powerful, but not many understand how powerful. You can keep many alive when instead they should be meetin' their own ancestors. This healin' magic mixed with the ability of Fortitude are a very powerful combination of spells. You remember this. It helpful to all manner of people: warriors, mages and everything in between.","done":"Good, then Kor'ja lives and goes off to defend our town from those malicious humans. I often wish to remember days of battle; where power was shown in combat and it was the wise who often destroyed those who relied on just their strength.\nYou done good by me, ‹name›. You take this robe now. Maybe it help, maybe you not care, but you earned it and I'm proud to call you brother.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":54.3,"y":42.9,"n":"Tai'jin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"5728":{"id":5728,"t":"Hidden Enemies","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,350 experience instead of 1,150, 2.04 times as much. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Kill Bazzalan and Jergosh the Invoker before returning to Thrall in Orgrimmar.\nBazzalan slain\nJergosh the Invoker slain","desc":"Hmm, leaders of the Searing Blade... this concerns me most. If they are the ones of value to Neeru, then those are who we must target first. This satyr... Bazzalan, and the other Neeru mentioned--what was he, a warlock?--must be slain.\nReturn to the Cleft of Shadow and enter Ragefire Chasm, ‹name›. Find these two leaders of the Searing Blade, and kill them. But be careful not to let Neeru know it was you who did this. You must retain your identity as one of his brothers/sisters in arms.","rew":"Money: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,350\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Have you found them yet, ‹name›? The leaders of the Searing Blade.\nI knew the Shadow Council sought to take Orgrimmar and all of the Horde from me, but I hadn't realized how quickly they were able to infiltrate the city. So many arms this beast has... we can cut them off until exhaustion sets in, but we will be no further than when we started. I will have to have my spies double their efforts.","done":"I am glad you've returned, ‹name›. Some of those loyal to me brought word immediately that the caverns below Orgrimmar were in disarray now that their leaders have been slain. I even heard reports that Neeru was more than agitated. It seems we've put a dent in his armor. I can't say I'm displeased... even with such a minor victory.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ragefire-chasm"]},"128":{"id":128,"t":"Blackrock Bounty","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 15 Blackrock Champions and Guard Howe in Lakeshire will reward you.\nBlackrock Champion slain : 0/ 15","desc":"The Blackrock Clan must be destroyed. The Enemy has invaded our lands. These mountains fall under the sovereign right of the King of Stormwind. Our sources tell us that the leaders of each unit within the Clan are known as Champions. You'll find them in their encampment to the north, just west of the road to the Burning Steppes.\nMagistrate Solomon wants these foul brutes dead. Slay 15 Blackrock Champions and return to me.","rew":"Money: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,000\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Return once you have slain 15 Blackrock Champions.","done":"I see you have fought valiantly against the Blackrock Clan, ‹class›. Your service to our township is great indeed.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":26.5,"y":57.9,"n":"Guard Howe","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"3088":{"id":3088,"t":"Encrypted Parchment","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Encrypted Parchment and speak to Rwag in the Valley of Trials.\nEncrypted Parchment\nProvided: Encrypted Parchment","desc":"Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, ‹name›.\nRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the rogue trainer Rwag. He would have words with you when you're ready.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Shhh, not so loud. I don't trust Nartok over there. Anyone that has to hide deeper in a cave than I do shouldn't be trifled with.\nI trust you had no problem finding your way around?","done":"Now that you know where I'm holding up, I should let you know: the Shattered Hand's asked me to look out for you. They want me to train you and keep you informed of anything they might need. Even if you're not interested in helping them yet--which you'd be a fool not to be--I'll do what I can to train you... for a small fee. Come back to me anytime you think you're ready, and we'll see what you're ready to learn.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":41.3,"y":68,"n":"Rwag","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"2608":{"id":2608,"t":"The Touch of Zanzil","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 160 experience instead of 150, 1.07 times as much.","obj":"/Lay down to be examined by Doc Mixilpixil. How can he find the cure if he can't find the cause?","desc":"Oh my, you look like death. Correction - I've seen death, you look worse than death. You, sir/miss, would be what death coughed up at his last physical.\nHah! You hear that Noarm? Write that one down!\n*Cough* Hrm yes, in order for me to help you, I'll need to draw some blood. Don't worry, it only hurts the first few... fifty times or so... /lay down when you're ready for the treatment, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 160","back":"When you're ready for the examination, /lay down on the ground and I'll begin the phlebotomy.","done":"Give me a moment to confer with my colleagues, ‹name›. Dr. Montgomery, Mr. Noarm, let us conference!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.1,"y":69.9,"n":"Doc Mixilpixil","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"7728":{"id":7728,"t":"STOLEN: Smithing Tuyere and Lookout's Spyglass","lv":48,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find and return the Smithing Tuyere and Lookout's Spyglass to Taskmaster Scrange in the Searing Gorge.\nThe only information you have about these items is the following: They were definitely stolen by Dark Iron dwarves. The Smithing Tuyere is a blacksmithing tool used by blacksmiths and the Lookout's Spyglass is an invaluable monitoring tool to lookouts.\nSmithing Tuyere Dark Iron Steamsmith 10 %\nLookout's Spyglass Dark Iron Lookout 10 %","desc":"The following items have been stolen:\n*One Dark Iron Tuyere.\n*One Lookout's Spyglass.\nA reward is being offered to individuals who find and return these pilfered items.\nThe Thorium Brotherhood is certain that these items were stolen by unscrupulous and jealous Dark Iron dwarves that inhabit the Searing Gorge.\nThe spyglass in question was an excellent tool for the lookouts and the tuyere was an irreplaceable smithing tool.\nShould you find the missing items, return them to Scrange.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSlagplate Leggings Everwarm Handwraps\nMoney: 1 40 1 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"If you're here for the reward, you're gonna have to give me the stolen goods.","done":"Fantastic work! Now for your reward.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":37.6,"y":26.5,"n":"Wanted/Missing/Lost & Found","s":1},{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":39,"y":27.5,"n":"Taskmaster Scrange","e":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8768":{"id":8768,"t":"A Gaily Wrapped Present","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nGaily Wrapped Present","done":"This festively-wrapped present has your name on it.\nWait, did it just move?\nDun Morogh Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.5,"y":31.8,"n":"Gaily Wrapped Present","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.3,"y":69.2,"n":"Gaily Wrapped Present","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"9248":{"id":9248,"t":"A Humble Offering","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Aurel Goldleaf at Cenarion Hold in Silithus wants you to bring her 1 Abyssal Scepter. You must also be Honored with the Cenarion Circle.\nAbyssal Scepter Prince Skaldrenox , High Marshal Whirlaxis , Baron Kazum , Lord Skwol\nReach 9000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"Ishnu-alah, ‹race›. Show me proof of the demise of a Lord of the Abyssal Council and I shall reward you with an item that should aid you in your battles against the Qiraji.","rew":"You will receive:\nBand of Cenarius\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Fandu-dath-belore? Oh, pardon me, ‹name›. I did not recognize you. Have you the scepter?","done":"Ande'thoras-ethil. It means; 'May your troubles be diminished,' in my native tongue.\nWear the band proudly and in good health, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Aurel Goldleaf","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"448":{"id":448,"t":"Report to Hadrec","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher.","desc":"Before you launch an assault on Fenris Isle, report to High Executor Hadrec. He may have additional information or equipment you'll need.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Coarse Weightstone 5 Coarse Sharpening Stone\nYou will also receive:\nMedium Armor Kit\nExperience: 575\n+50 reputation with Undercity","done":"If what Bethor says is true then Thule Ravenclaw is a force that must be dealt with, and dealt with soon.\nTo aid in this task, you may take something from our arsenal here...","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.9,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":40.9,"n":"High Executor Hadrec","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"1088":{"id":1088,"t":"Ordanus","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ordanus' head to Braelyn Firehand near Sun Rock Retreat.\nOrdanus' Head Keeper Ordanus","desc":"They thought that they could halt the flow of magic. They were mistaken. They thought that they could hide Ordanus, but I will have his head!\nMagic grants me true sight. Yes... there he is. A crossroads... At the top of a great tree in Ashenvale Forest. A name... Raynewood. One of the eldest sons of the forest god. They spirited him away from the peak before I could find him, but his time runs short.\nBring it to me and I will share with you a mighty gift.","rew":"Experience: 2,350","back":"When my master bade me to the peak of Stonetalon, I expected that all I would need was to lay waste to the night elves that crawled the sacred ruins of our ancient temple of Azshara, their touch despoiling its sanctity... but Ordanus had slipped my grasp.","done":"I knew Ordanus once, long ago. He had the arrogance of his kind, holding himself above even the Highborne.\nHis head does not rise so high now, does it, ‹name›?\nI promised you a reward, and you shall have it. Attend to me.\nStonetalon Mountains Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":45.9,"y":60.4,"n":"Braelyn Firehand","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"1248":{"id":1248,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":33,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Mikhail in the Wetlands.","desc":"A contact of mine retired in the Wetlands at the harbor city of Menethil. He should be willing to help on your word alone if you tell him you're working for me. His name is Mikhail. He mentioned becoming a bartender before leaving Stormwind a few years ago.\nSpeak to him, find this Slim, and find out if there's anything else to know about this kidnapped diplomat. We need to find out where they've taken him, or at least who he is. The docket doesn't mention anything about their plans after he's captured.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Welcome, welcome, welcome, ‹name›. Good of you to join us. Perhaps an ale today? Or some mutton?\nName your pleasure and I'll see to it that you're taken care of. My name is Mikhail, and I look forward to serving you.\nHmm? What's that? Trias? Keep your voice down, my friend. This isn't something for the whole tavern to hear about.\nStormwind City Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":66,"y":74.1,"n":"Elling Trias","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.6,"y":60.8,"n":"Mikhail","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"97328":{"id":97328,"t":"Anything of value","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Recover 8 Stolen Shipments from the Ruins of Zul'Kunda in Stranglethorn Vale and return your haul to someone in Booty Bay.\n8 Stolen Shipment","desc":"<As you sift through the debris left behind by a horrible zeppelin crash directly above, you find evidence of a hefty shipment of supplies that has long since been plundered of all its value. Even the shipping labels have been torn and shredded, leaving only the words 'Booty Bay' barely legible on one.\nCountless two-toed footprints and several patches of divotted earth all lead toward ruins in the northwest.>","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 97328","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"208":{"id":208,"t":"Big Game Hunter","lv":43,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Master Hunter's Wand, Master Hunter's Spellsword.","obj":"Hemet Nesingwary wants you to bring him the head of King Bangalash, the great white tiger.\nHead of Bangalash King Bangalash","desc":"‹name›, you are a hunter worthy of our company. From the battlefields of Lordaeron to the deepest jungle, I have rarely witnessed such prowess with weaponry as you have demonstrated.\nYou have killed the ferocious Sin'Dall, the elusive Bag'thera and the treacherous Tethis. But the true prize is the head of King Bangalash. That white tiger is the reason I am here. I've had my sights on him for quite some time now. Kill King Bangalash and your hunting prowess is proven to be second to none.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMaster Hunter's Bow Master Hunter's Rifle Master Hunter's Wand Master Hunter's Spellsword\nNew in Forever: Master Hunter's Wand, Master Hunter's Spellsword.\nExperience: 5,350","back":"I see you're back, old bloke. King Bangalash has caused me to come crawling back to camp many times. Hang in there.","done":"Bloody well done! Right-o! Congratulations, ‹name›, for succeeding where others have failed.\nI am honored to count you as a comrade of our great hunting party here. No one will ever doubt your expertise in hunting and tracking!\nCheers to you, I say! Cheers!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.7,"y":10.8,"n":"Hemet Nesingwary","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"608":{"id":608,"t":"The Bloodsail Buccaneers","lv":45,"min":37,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fleet-Master Seahorn in Booty Bay wants you to kill Captain Stillwater, Captain Keelhaul and Fleet Master Firallon.\nCaptain Stillwater slain\nCaptain Keelhaul slain\nFleet Master Firallon slain","desc":"Blast the nerve of Firallon! He couldn't sail a skiff through Crystal Lake let alone lead an entire fleet against us.\nThe Bloodsail Buccaneers will pay for their carelessness. Now that we know their plan of attack, we can counter before they know what hit them.\nBut why send the entire fleet to do the work of one brave adventuring party? ‹name›, take some of your most skilled comrades out to Firallon's landing spot and assassinate the Bloodsail leadership. Their fleet will sink soon after....","rew":"You will receive:\nBlackwater Tunic\nExperience: 4,850\n+150 reputation with Booty Bay\n-750 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"What's the problem, ‹name›? We need to attack before the Bloodsail Buccaneers do!","done":"Ah, what a great day for the Blackwater Raiders! Three cheers to you, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.2,"y":77,"n":"Fleet Master Seahorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8928":{"id":8928,"t":"A Shifty Merchant","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search for an imp inside a cave at the entrance of Darkwhisper Gorge in southern Winterspring, purchase a Fel Elemental Rod and return to Mux Manascrambler in Gadgetzan.\nFel Elemental Rod sold by Vi'el","desc":"The core will provide us with enough juice to power our device; now we just have to build a rod that can channel that energy without melting.\nI met an imp in Winterspring that sold all manner of exotic goods. He had an elemental rod that would do perfectly. I'm kicking myself in the head right now for not having bought it.\nHe lives inside a cave in the entrance to Darkwhisper Gorge. Sneak in there and try to find him.\nMake sure he only charges you forty gold; that's the price he quoted me!","rew":"Experience: 3,300","back":"Have you had any luck finding the imp in Darkwhisper Gorge?","done":"You did it! This rod will do perfectly. Now to put it all together...\nTanaris Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Mux Manascrambler","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"928":{"id":928,"t":"Crown of the Earth","lv":5,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Partially Filled Vessel to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.\nPartially Filled Vessel\nProvided: Partially Filled Vessel","desc":"While there is more I could speak to you of the moonwells and of Teldrassil, I must send you along. Corithras Moonrage will be expecting you. I have poured the phial of water you brought to me into this vessel to bring to him.\nSeek out Corithras. You will find him at the moonwell in Dolanaar. Follow the road south from Aldrassil out of Shadowglen, and continue to follow the cobblestones as the road turns west.\nMind you stay on the road though, ‹name›. There are dangerous beasts in the forests of late.","rew":"Experience: 230\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Greetings, ‹class›. For what purpose do I owe the pleasure of our meeting?","done":"Ah, I see. You were sent by Tenaron. Well then, it would seem we have much to talk about, much to do, and little time to do it in.\nI think we'd best get started.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":59.1,"y":39.4,"n":"Tenaron Stormgrip","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.1,"y":61.7,"n":"Corithras Moonrage","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"848":{"id":848,"t":"Fungal Spores","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Fungal Spores to Apothecary Helbrim at the Crossroads.\n4 Fungal Spores Laden Mushroom","desc":"The oases of the Barrens hide a mystery. Life energy flows from their waters, invigorating the plants and beasts that drink it.\nInvigorating, and altering.\nThere is a mushroom that grows near these oases. Its spores hold properties that we, the apothecaries of Lordaeron, find useful.\nBring me these spores and you will earn our gratitude.","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do you have the spores, ‹name›? There is a concoction I must send to my associate in Thunder Bluff, which requires the spores...","done":"Ah, yes. These are good specimens. Potent.\nI am Forsaken, and we honor our contracts. Here is your reward, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.4,"y":30.2,"n":"Apothecary Helbrim","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"5088":{"id":5088,"t":"Arikara","lv":28,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Smouldering Leggings.","obj":"Slay Arikara. Bring her remains and the Incendia powder to Motega Firemane in Whitereach Post as proof of your deed.\nIncendia Powder\nArikara Serpent Skin Arikara\nProvided: Incendia Powder","desc":"Take this refined and purified Incendia powder to Thousand Needles and toss it on the sacred fire of life. It is located in the Darkcloud Pinnacle on an isolated needle where they bury their dead.\nThe enchantment that I have weaved into the Incendia powder will summon Arikara to you, ‹name›.\nI fear she may be stalking Cairne Bloodhoof; too much Tauren lore has changed, and I fear this has angered Arikara. Move quickly before all is lost, ‹class›!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBrute Hammer Stingshot Wand Clink Shield Smouldering Leggings\nNew in Forever: Smouldering Leggings.\nMoney: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,300\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Have you slain the vicious serpent Arikara, ‹name›?","done":"This does not make sense. Why would Arikara be after Cairne Bloodhoof? Magatha could not be wrong, she is our most powerful shaman.\n<Motega shakes his head.>\nRegardless, your great deed to the Horde shall not go unnoticed - please, choose one of these as a reward for your aid.\nThunder Bluff Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":69.9,"y":30.9,"n":"Magatha Grimtotem","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":21.5,"y":32.3,"n":"Motega Firemane","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"768":{"id":768,"t":"Gathering Leather","lv":8,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 12 pieces of Light Leather to Veren Tallstrider in Thunder Bluff.\n12 Light Leather Tattered Chest 18 % , Battered Chest 18 % , Armor Crate 0 % , Tattered Chest 0 % and 4 more","desc":"Greetings, young one. You have a gleam in your eye; I can tell you are eager to venture back to the plains for the hunt. May you bring honor to your clan!\nI work with the skins of beasts, fashioning them into clothes and armor for the people of Thunder Bluff.\nIf you hunt beasts and bring me their skins, then I will fashion something for you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAnimal Skin Belt Double-layered Gloves\nExperience: 875\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Hello again. Have you been hunting? Do you have skins for me?","done":"Ah, these are very nice pieces. They'll make fine leather goods.\nHere, ‹name›. Take this in trade...\nThunder Bluff Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":44.4,"y":44.7,"n":"Veren Tallstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"368":{"id":368,"t":"A New Plague","lv":9,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Apothecary Johaan of the town of Brill needs 5 Vile Fin Scales from Murlocs in Tirisfal Glades.\n5 Vile Fin Scale Vile Fin Tidecaller 40 % , Vile Fin Shorecreeper 40 % , Vile Fin Lakestalker 40 % , Vile Fin Oracle 40 % and 4 more","desc":"While you were collecting samples for me, my experiments led me to realize that more reagents will be required for this new disease to spread properly. Poisoning some hapless victim is child's play. Plaguing an entire world proves to be a bit more complicated.\nI will need 5 Vile Fin Scales from Murlocs in the vicinity. You will find the creatures along the coast to the north or to the west.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Slumber Sand\nMoney: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 775\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"‹name›, were you able to obtain 5 Vile Fin Scales from the Murlocs?","done":"The scales are perfect, ‹name›. Exactly what I needed for this concoction.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":59.4,"y":52.4,"n":"Apothecary Johaan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"95328":{"id":95328,"t":"Whispering horror residue","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver Whispering Horror Residue to Father Lankester in the War Quarter of Undercity.\nWhispering Horror Residue","desc":"Against your better judgement you scrape up and collect the squirming remains of the beast. Someone in Undercity might have a use for them.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do you have something for me, ‹class›?","done":"What an interesting specimen. From underneath the Whispering Forest, you say? It's no secret that foul place is touched by the void.\nI welcome the opportunity to explore the mysteries of shadow, ‹class›. Allow me to offer you payment for what you've found.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":49.6,"y":15.6,"n":"Father Lankester","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4288":{"id":4288,"t":"The Western Pylon","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Discover the location of the Western Crystal Pylon.","desc":"My experiments so far have not yielded any positive results, ‹name›. I can't help but hope that you can find a solution by searching for one of the pylons that I have heard exist.\nPerhaps if we combine certain colors at them... but I get ahead of myself. Let's find them first!\n‹name›, search the western area of the crater; a pylon is said to be somewhere in that area.","rew":"Experience: 3,950","back":"Have you visited the pylon, ‹name›?","done":"There are many hidden areas of the crater along the sides. Try exploring the winding paths if you can't think of anywhere else to look, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":41.9,"y":2.7,"n":"J.D. Collie","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"3568":{"id":3568,"t":"Seeping Corruption","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fill all 4 Empty Vials at the tide pools along the coast of the Ruins of Eldarath in Azshara before returning to Chemist Cuely.\nFilled Vial Labeled #1\nFilled Vial Labeled #2\nFilled Vial Labeled #3\nFilled Vial Labeled #4\nProvided: Box of Empty Vials","desc":"See that tauren behind me--the one who looks like she's going to be ill at any moment? She was in Azshara recently. She claims she was wounded by some naga while making her way through the Ruins of Eldarath.\nAfter fighting off a few of them, she took a break on the beach and drank from one of the tide pools. Now she's feeling nauseous... among other things.\nI'd like to find out what she drank. Take this box, in it are some empty vials I labeled. Fill each at different pools and come back.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"You know where this is leading, don't you, ‹name›? There's no way she can survive... look at her. The best thing for her now is to aid us in finding a cure for the plague. This water she drank might have a clue that helps us figure out how. She's going to die anyway--she might as well die doing something noble for our people before she does. Don't you agree?","done":"Wonderful. You're back before she died. Good, good.\nLet's get started on this then, shall we?\nI've been studying her symptoms for some time now, and it's quite ugly. I'm surprised she's still standing. She's vomited three or four times all over the place... quite a pleasant odor.\nGive me just a moment to put something together to test on our... friend.\nUndercity Azshara","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":48.7,"y":71.4,"n":"Chemist Cuely","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"8368":{"id":8368,"t":"Battle of Warsong Gulch","lv":19,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","rew":"Money: 11 0 gold, 11 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,450\n+100 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","done":"Excellent! You've shown your worth by defending our operations in Warsong Gulch! May word of your honor spread far and wide across our lands.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5408":{"id":5408,"t":"Minion's Scourgestones","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Minion's Scourgestone Skeletal Terror 50 % , Slavering Ghoul 50 % , Hungering Wraith 50 % , Foulmane 50 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nArgent Dawn Valor Token\nExperience: 550\n+25 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"A Minion's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge rank and file. These are sometimes found on the weaker of their troops positioned in the Plaguelands, though the term \"weaker\" is certainly to be considered in context. The Scourge, no matter where they are, should never be underestimated.\nThe Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for twenty of these insignia - an exchange I'm happy to do, provided you have earned enough scourgestones!","done":"Congratulations, ‹name› - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!\nThe tokens serve two purposes. One - they can be used to further your standing within the Argent Dawn; to do so may avail you options and rewards that are reserved for our honored and revered allies. Two - they can be given to our quartermasters, along with coin, as payment for some of the Dawn's more prized items.\nWhatever you decide, know that you are earning your commission. Well done!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.2,"y":68.4,"n":"Argent Officer Garush","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"79008":{"id":79008,"t":"And that note you found","lv":22,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Charred remains of the note serve as your only guide.","desc":"<The faint radiance of the embers darkening, you stumble across the remnants of a recent fire.\nAmidst the scattered provisions, you discover a blistered note.>\n\"Not all that burns is lost. Find the twin land, find the place.\"","rew":"You will receive:\nSwiftness Potion Lesser Troll's Blood Elixir\nExperience: 1,750","done":"As you stumble upon the remnants of yet another charred corpse, your gaze falls upon a message secured to a wooden plank.\nWestfall The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":37.5,"y":50.7,"n":"Burned-Out Remains","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.4,"y":73.9,"n":"Burned-Out Remains","e":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.4,"y":73.8,"n":"Nailed Plank","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"48":{"id":48,"t":"Sweet Amber","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Holy Spring Water to Grimbooze Thunderbrew.\nHoly Spring Water The Holy Spring","desc":"In the land to the south where vines twist and creep\nLies a hidden well where the water runs deep\nPure as the Light's sacred Daughter\nBring to me now some Holy Spring Water.","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,750","back":"Hiccup! Ho ho! You want an encore?\nIn the land to the south where vines twist and creep\nLies a hidden well where the water runs deep\nPure as the Light's sacred Daughter\nBring to me now some Holy Spring Water.","done":"Hiccup! Ho Ho!\nWestfall Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":44.6,"y":80.3,"n":"Grimbooze Thunderbrew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"288":{"id":288,"t":"The Third Fleet","lv":27,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Buy First Mate Fitzsimmons a Flagon of Mead.\nFlagon of Dwarven Honeymead Malgin Barleybrew 75 % , sold by Roberto Pupellyverbos , sold by Barkeep Dobbins , sold by Julia Gallina and 4 more","desc":"I was once First Mate on the Wave Mistress, ship-of-the-line in the Kul Tiras Third Fleet. The Doomed Fleet. Doomed, for on its last voyage the fleet was attacked by Red Dragons. Dragons controlled by Orcs!\nWe didn't stand a chance against that dragonfire...and our fleet was burned and sunk off this here coast. I'm the sole survivor of those poor vessels...\n...Oh, my head hammers and pounds! I'll need a fresh drink if I'm to get a handle on this hangover and continue my tale.","rew":"Experience: 220","back":"Oh, I'm so very thirsty! Won't you buy a drink for this poor, pathetic fool?","done":"Ah! That hits the spot, and loosens the tongue. Thanks, mate!","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.9,"y":59.6,"n":"First Mate Fitzsimmons","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"98208":{"id":98208,"t":"Bloom of the heavens","lv":29,"min":22,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Recover Nord'el for Sylessa Duskwhisper in Menethil Harbor.\nNord'el","desc":"I came to Menethil Harbor from Auberdine, from the great tree Teldrassil, to recover a bloom of great import to my people.\nMy people's ship the Flying Osprey crashed here many moons ago, joined with the Kul Tiran Third Fleet. Among its cargo was the flower known as Nord'el--Bloom of the Heavens in your tongue--bloomed under a full moon at the peak of Mount Hyjal, our former home.\nPlease help me retrieve it! The wreckage is just south of the city, but it is inhabited by fierce murloc raiders!","rew":"You will receive:\nBouquet of Auberdine Flowers\nMoney: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,350\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":8,"y":55.8,"n":"Sylessa Duskwhisper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92528":{"id":92528,"t":"Among the faithful","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Look around Falaath Village to learn about the cult's intentions in the Shen'dar Highlands.\nLearn about the cultists' plans","desc":"The faithful of Al'Akir grow ever stronger with each eager new recruit like yourself. As you can see, our strength gives form to the storm itself!\nNormally I'd send you straight to Skypriest Aanders for assessment, but he is occupied at present receiving a guest at the inn on the north side of town. Please avoid that place for now. An unshaven recruit like yourself in the presence of such a guest would be inappropriate.\nFor now, just don't get in anyone's way.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nStained Ritual Dagger Curved Scimitar Windswept Shortbow\nExperience: 350","back":"What did you learn?","done":"Lorthuna herself was there? She's the leader of the whole damned cult!\nIf they are making a move on Shen'dar Village and the western watchtower, we've got to be ready. What is strange is... why the watchtower?\nThe Village I can understand, but the tower? It doesn't have much strategic significance, other than as a minor lookout post.\nRegardless, we will be prepared for them. They'll find that highlanders aren't as easy to catch flat footed as they might think.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":46.8,"y":56.2,"n":"Missionary Jasaan","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.6,"y":45.4,"n":"Constable Aonda","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"2768":{"id":2768,"t":"Divino-matic Rod","lv":47,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Divino-matic Rod to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan.\nDivino-matic Rod Sergeant Bly in Zul'Farrak","desc":"Sergeant Bly stole from me! He said he'd only borrow it, but he stole my cherished divino-matic rod!! Without that rod how will I know where to dig new water holes??\nFind Bly and bring me my rod! I heard he led his band of ill-reputed adventurers to go treasure hunting in Zul'Farrak to the west. I bet you'll find him there.\nLet's hope the trolls took care of him, because if you have to fight him for the rod then you're in for a serious fight.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMasons Fraternity Ring Engineer's Guild Headpiece\nExperience: 6,300\n+200 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Did you find Sergeant Bly? Did you get my divino-matic rod?","done":"You found it! Well done, ‹name›! Did you have to fight Bly for it? I hope you knocked him and his band down good and hard!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":28.5,"n":"Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulfarrak"]},"8048":{"id":8048,"t":"The Hero's Brand","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Heathen's Brand","rew":"You will receive:\nHero's Brand\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"The King has acknowledged your existence, ‹class›. You are the first of your kind to be accepted by Rastakhan as a true ally of Zandalar.\nYou will be rewarded greatly for your efforts. Present your brand and I shall apply the final amplification.","done":"Vigilance, honor, loyalty, bravery... You embody all of these traits and so shall your brand.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":14.4,"n":"Jin'rokh the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});